# Build context filter for the Spendy image.
#
# Strategy: DENY EVERYTHING, then re-allow exactly the three paths the image needs.
# Rationale: this repo sits in a Google Drive folder next to the owner's real financial
# data (spendy-db.js is ~61 MB of transactions and base64 receipt photos, and the meta
# blob holds card numbers + CVV). An allow-list is the only version of this file that
# stays correct when a new personal file appears in the folder tomorrow.
#
# Docker sends the Dockerfile itself to the builder regardless of the rules below.

# 1) Deny everything.
*

# 2) Re-allow only what the runtime image actually contains.
!Spendy.html
!spendy.js
!server

# 3) Belt and braces. Later patterns win, so nothing re-allowed above can smuggle these
#    in — and neither can a future edit to the allow-list.

# The owner's data, in every shape it takes
**/data
**/spendy-db.js
**/spendy-sync.json
**/backup
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.csv
**/*.zip
**/*.docx
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.webp
**/images
**/tmp

# Repo/agent scratch that has no business in an image layer
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.github
**/.codegraph
**/.claude
**/docs
**/screenshots
**/tasks
**/idea
**/*.md
**/NOTES.md
**/TODO.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Local config / editor / OS junk
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini
**/*.lnk
